{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK4VXXoBeP6NQ7Teg8bQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`FilePathField(path=...)` on a model can now take a callable, so the directory is worked out when the form field is built, not frozen into migrations.\n\n**The fix** is a one-line change in `django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1712`. When `formfield()` builds the form field, it now calls `self.path()` if `path` is callable and uses the value as-is otherwise. Because `deconstruct()` saves the callable itself, `makemigrations` writes a reference to your function, not the path it resolves to on your machine. In the issue's case you'd write:\n\n```python\ndef local_files_path():\n    return os.path.join(settings.LOCAL_FILE_DIR, 'example_dir')\n\nfile = models.FilePathField(path=local_files_path)\n```\n\nThe callable has to be a module-level function. Migrations can't serialize a lambda.\n\n**Docs:** I added a note and that example under `FilePathField.path` in `docs/ref/models/fields.txt`, marked `versionchanged:: 3.0`. I chose 3.0 as the version, so change it if this is going into a different release.\n\n**Tests:** the `model_fields` and `forms_tests.field_tests.test_filepathfield` suites pass (270 tests, 48 skipped). I didn't add a test for a callable path, since the rules said not to edit test files, so nothing here checks that case directly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":238,"cache_read_input_tokens":20197,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":238},"output_tokens":444,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fef88bba-e259-426e-b407-22da2e27143a","uuid":"8ae91176-a8b1-413c-9499-27fc3223b51f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:20:55.073Z","request_id":"req_011ChK4VXQ7LrnQjdETKHYUX"}
